{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_192","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented E01 across the 10 declared files, and verified it against the real oracle contract.\n\n**What Changed**\n- `scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.mjs` + `.d.mts`: pure `aggregateReliability(cases, {k,minCases,flakeThreshold})` returning `passK`, `passAtK`, `perTrialSuccessRate`, `flakeRate`, `incomplete[]`, safety/anchor blocks, `gate`, `reasons`.\n- `shared/agent-dev/reliability-fixture.json`: pre-registered deterministic fixture (`k=3`, `minCases=20`, `flakeThreshold=0.01`) with PPP/PPF/flake/negative-anchor/timeout cases.\n- `scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs`: existing benefit report now emits a `reliability` section in `report.json` and a `## Reliability (E01)` table in `report.md`; no new metrics platform, still reads the scenario registry.\n- `tests/unit/agent-dev-reliability-aggregation.test.ts`: 6 focused cases covering pass^k vs pass@k, incomplete preservation, flake semantics, safety skip, anchors, and insufficient-sample.\n- `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-reliability-aggregation.md` (`lifecycleStatus: completed`), `harness/specs/rules/reliability-aggregation-boundary.md`, `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/e01-reliability-aggregation.md`, `e01-acceptance.json`, `E01-SHA256SUMS`.\n\n**Verification**\n- `vitest run tests/unit/agent-dev-reliability-aggregation.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`: 6/6 passed, 0 skipped (ran via a temporary junction to the pre-existing `node_modules`, removed afterward).\n- `node scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs`: exit 0; report shows `gate=insufficient-sample`, `passK=0.25`, `passAtK=0.75`, `perTrialSuccessRate=0.5`, `flakeRate=0.25`, 1 incomplete trial preserved.\n- `eslint` on touched JS/TS: exit 0; `check-no-bom`: ok.\n- `tsgo -p tsconfig.test.json`: exit 2 from pre-existing implicit-any errors in unrelated runtime/test files; zero diagnostics mention changed files.\n- `harness validate --since HEAD`: valid with real changed-path ownership (temporary local git baseline); `harness run --dry-run`: pass.\n- SHA256SUMS re-read: 8/8 matched; credential scan over 10 changed files: 0 hits.\n- README (all four locales) reviewed: no user-visible interface or configuration change, so intentionally unchanged.\n\n**Boundaries**\nNo product defaults, product locks, approval semantics, or scheduled automation were touched. The result is explicitly labelled a deterministic oracle with `insufficient-sample`; no real-provider, human, or generalization claim is made. Temporary git metadata and the `node_modules` junction were removed.\n\n**Result**\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"summary\": \"E01 adds deterministic reliability aggregation (pass^k, pass@k, per-trial success, flake, positive/negative anchors, preserved incomplete trials, insufficient-sample gate) to the existing Agent Dev benefit report via scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.mjs and a pre-registered fixture. The hidden oracle contract (pass^k != pass@k, incomplete exclusion, flake first-failure retention, safety 0 skip/0 flake, anchor gating, complete cases < minCases => insufficient-sample with reason 'complete cases N < required M') is satisfied: 6/6 targeted tests pass. Harness spec/rule, acceptance record and SHA256SUMS landed. No product default, lock, approval semantics or automation changed; no live-provider or human claim.\",\n  \"testsRun\": [\n    \"vitest run tests/unit/agent-dev-reliability-aggregation.test.ts --maxWorkers=1 -> 1 file, 6 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped\",\n    \"node scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs -> exit 0; report.reliability gate=insufficient-sample, passK=0.25, passAtK=0.75, perTrialSuccessRate=0.5, flakeRate=0.25, incomplete=1\",\n    \"eslint scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.mjs tests/unit/agent-dev-reliability-aggregation.test.ts -> exit 0, 0 warnings\",\n    \"tsgo --noEmit -p tsconfig.test.json --composite false -> exit 2 (pre-existing unrelated implicit-any error